{"id": "b64f5f6e2995", "ts": "2026-10-21T16:49:48", "event": "tool_call", "tool": "get_electrical_specs", "permission": "read-only", "server": "table-register", "args": {"chip": "esp32", "parameter": "deep-sleep"}, "latency_ms": 0, "error": null, "session": "web"}
{"id": "e92d8c0a1620", "ts": "2026-10-21T16:49:50", "event": "answer", "qid": "671777eb", "session": "web", "status": "answered", "latency_s": 4.021, "verified": true, "answer": "The ESP32 deep-sleep current consumption with the RTC timer and RTC memory enabled is **10 µA** (typical) [ESP32_Datasheet p.45, ESP32_Low_Power_AppNote p.6]. \n\nTo achieve and maintain this 10 µA deep-sleep level:\n* Unused GPIO pins should be isolated using `rtc_gpio_isolate()` to prevent leakage currents through internal pull-up or pull-down resistors [ESP32_Low_Power_AppNote p.6].\n* Flash and external PSRAM should be powered down before entering deep sleep [ESP32_Low_Power_AppNote p.6].\n* *(No"}
