{"id": "f0ad3fb79c99", "ts": "2026-10-24T08:49:15", "event": "answer", "qid": "d698026e", "session": "web", "status": "answered", "latency_s": 16.584, "verified": true, "answer": "When there is insufficient FreeRTOS heap memory available to allocate the task data structures (TCB) and stack, **`xTaskCreate()`** returns:\n\n```c\nerrCOULD_NOT_ALLOCATE_REQUIRED_MEMORY\n```\n\n*(defined as `-1` in `projdefs.h`, which is distinct from `pdPASS` / `pdTRUE` which equals `1`)* [FreeRTOS_Ref_Manual p.30–31].\n\n### Additional Details:\n* **Success return value:** `pdPASS` (indicates the task was created successfully) [FreeRTOS_Ref_Manual p.30].\n* **Trapping heap allocation failures:** If `h"}
